  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "##Representing Input and Output with Flowcharts\r\n\r\nExplore the flowchart provided in the sketch on this level. Trace two different user paths  from start to end. Label where your function gets information (inputs), shows results (outputs), and makes yes/no decisions that change the path.\r\n\r\n:::details [What's a user path?]\r\nThink about how you would label the chart to represent a specific cake. For example, how would you model a user ordering a **Chocolate Fudge Cake that says \"Happy Birthday\"**?\r\n:::\r\n",
